      "url": "https://mariaadey.com/2026/11/09/rohr-lake-backpacking-trip/",
      "title": "[The Road Goes Ever On] Rohr Lake Backpacking Trip",
      "content_html": "<img src=\"https://mariaadey.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/55643426929_017e24b2d7_b-e1794258139785.jpg\" style=\"width:100%;max-height:300px;object-fit:cover;\"/>\n<p style=\"margin:0 0 0.75em;padding:5px 10px;background:#f0f4f8;border-left:3px solid #7b9fc4;border-radius:3px;font-size:0.82em;color:#444;line-height:1.8;\">🌾 🔧 🌲 <a href=\"https://zirnhelt.github.io/super-rss-feed/review.html?url=https%3A%2F%2Fmariaadey.com%2F2026%2F11%2F09%2Frohr-lake-backpacking-trip%2F\" style=\"color:#7b9fc4;text-decoration:none;\">✏️</a></p>\nThe author completed a one-night backpacking trip to Rohr Lake over Thanksgiving weekend despite fresh snow and temperatures reaching -5°C. The 4.5-kilometre hike involved 500 metres of elevation gain and a challenging, slippery boulder field. She camped in the forest for warmth, enjoyed a campfire and clear stars, and returned safely using microspikes.",
